ak:attribute id="17" inc="1">Poisonous plants</groundspeak:attribute></groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:difficulty>3</groundspeak:difficulty><groundspeak:terrain>2</groundspeak:terrain><groundspeak:country>United States</groundspeak:country><groundspeak:state>Ohio</groundspeak:state><groundspeak:short_description>
</groundspeak:short_description><groundspeak:long_description>&lt;p&gt;This cache is located inside Turningbridge Park in Liberty Township, Butler County. This 45-acre park features a paved walking path for hiking, biking, and wildlife viewing. You can see a &lt;a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4IwCUj4rFxw"&gt;video of the path here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The address to the park is 5889 Laurel Run Drive, Liberty Township, OH 45011.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Liberty Twp is the smallest of the townships in Butler County. The township was named after Liberty, PA at the suggestion of John Morrow, a resident in the township at the time of its formation in 1803. Mr. Marrow was the brother of Ohio Governor Jeremiah Morrow.  The first settler of the township was John Nelson who arrived in 1796, seven years before Ohio became a state. There are some rather large trees in this area so they may have seen Mr. Nelson?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There are 25 Liberty Townships in the state of Ohio. &lt;/p&gt;

</groundspeak:long_description><groundspeak:encoded_hints /><groundspeak:logs><groundspeak:log id="1322747273"><groundspeak:date>2025-09-06T14:20:13</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Didn't find it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="5649378">DRJDSmith</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">After a great day golfing with my buddy, I wanted to snag a few caches before heading home. I went after the three along this bike path, but was only able to find two. Enjoyed walking the bike path and getting some steps. 

From the pictures of past finders the container looks like the same one from the first cache in this series. But, I was unable to find it. This one might be better to look for after the foliage has gone. </groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1303326258"><groundspeak:date>2025-06-07T12:16:22</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Didn't find it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="2774976">ohioyeti</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">we walked around the GZ twice and could not find any foot trail into the brush that is easily hip high on an adult. This one’s gonna have to wait for a fall day.</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1285559401"><groundspeak:date>2025-03-15T12:38:08</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="2012458">abney33</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Found it on the second try a few months after the first try. Log is dry and in good shape.</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1266739666"><groundspeak:date>2024-10-21T18:00:19</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Didn't find it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="2012458">abney33</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">We looked in the area. GPS doesn’t give exact coordinates. Jumps from 1 ft to 14 feet away with one step</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1236709499"><groundspeak:date>2024-05-26T22:02:02</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Didn't find it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="21509908">vdixon88</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Looked but could not find it </groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log></groundspeak:logs></groundspeak:cache></wpt><wpt lat="39.40527436635578" lon="-84.42425608634949"><time>2021-06-19T17:18:20</time><name>P09CZH8</name><cmt>20 spot parking lot for this nice community park.</cmt><desc>Turningbridge Park Parking</desc><url>https://www.geocaching.com/seek/wpt.aspx?WID=200396bf-10dc-4340-adc0-20331b40b479</url><urlname>Turningbridge Park Parking</urlname><sym>Parking Area</sym><type>Waypoint|Parking Area</type></wpt></gpx>